        "text": "Page: Louis le Brocquy Táin illustrations. Sentence: It tells of the exploits of King Conchobar and his chief warrior Cúchulainn (\"The Hound of Ulster\") and of the invasion of Ulster by Queen Medb of Connacht in an attempt to capture the Brown Bull of Cuailgne.\nPage: Ulster. Sentence: Ulster ( ; Irish: \"Ulaidh\" ] or \"Cúige Uladh\" ] , Ulster Scots: \"Ulstèr\" or \"Ulster\") is a province in the north of the island of Ireland.\nPage: Scots language. Sentence: Scots is the Germanic language variety spoken in Lowland Scotland and parts of Ulster (where the local dialect is known as Ulster Scots).\nPage: Aikenhead. Sentence: Aikenhead is a Scots language surname of medieval Scottish origin.",
